From: Richard T. Carback III <rick.carback@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: core: Add snps,keep-usb20-retry to clear GUCTL3 USB20_RETRY_DISABLE

On the ASUS Ascent QN10 (DWC_usb31 2.00a) GUCTL3.USB20_RETRY_DISABLE is
already set when Linux takes over, so the controller does not retry
USB2.0 transactions after an error. A HighSpeed hub behind the internal
Genesys hub then fails with -71 (SET_ADDRESS, port resets) under Linux,
while the same device works in UEFI.

Add an snps,keep-usb20-retry property that clears the bit.

Local test patch for the QN10 7.4-rc1 kernel build.
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
index d9f4e4109..0970d1efa 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -1534,6 +1534,18 @@ int dwc3_core_init(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 		dwc3_writel(dwc, DWC3_GUCTL3, reg);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Firmware may leave USB2.0 internal retries disabled. Boards whose
+	 * USB2 HS paths need retries (the ASUS Ascent QN10: a hub behind the
+	 * internal hub fails with -71 without them) clear the bit with
+	 * snps,keep-usb20-retry. This overrides the workaround above.
+	 */
+	if (device_property_read_bool(dwc->dev, "snps,keep-usb20-retry")) {
+		reg = dwc3_readl(dwc, DWC3_GUCTL3);
+		reg &= ~DWC3_GUCTL3_USB20_RETRY_DISABLE;
+		dwc3_writel(dwc, DWC3_GUCTL3, reg);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 
 err_power_off_phy:
